{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Discovered while fixing dbca-97ac-ad96-4d6d (potential-powellite-mouflon). This ticket is now **scoped to the one reachable, unambiguous site**; the two design-decision siblings were split out (see \"Split-out siblings\" below), following the /rebar-debug escalate-design-decisions guard.\n\n## Problem (in scope)\n`src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:541` raises a **bare** `WorkflowError(\"unknown scripted step {name!r} (not in the step registry)\")`. Because `WorkflowError` subclasses `LLMError`, `error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`, branch 7) maps it to `llm_unavailable`. An unknown scripted `uses:` step is a caller/plan-authoring fault, not an LLM outage.\n\n## Mechanism / reachability (proven, see Phase-1 RCA comment)\n- The linter (`lint_refs.py`) validates step shape/fields but NOT scripted-step registry membership, so an unknown `uses:` name passes lint and is only caught at execute time by this raise.\n- It reaches the classification seam through the generic MCP guard (`_mcp_errors._envelope_error`) and the LLM-tier gate surface (`_mcp_llm._structured_llm_failure`, used by review_plan/verify_completion/review_code/scan_spec). Runtime-confirmed: all three surfaces currently return `llm_unavailable`.\n\n## Contract violated\ndbca established the per-subclass taxonomy: a workflow that WAS found but is invalid (parse/lint/migrate) is caller `invalid_input`; only the bare execute base stays `llm_unavailable` (protects genuine execute-time outages, dbca AC3). An unknown `uses:` step is a found-but-invalid workflow — the same class as `WorkflowValidationError`→`invalid_input`. `invalid_input` is already in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (no new vocabulary).\n\n## Fix plan\n1. `src/rebar/llm/errors.py`: add `WorkflowUnknownStepError(WorkflowError)` — a caller/plan-authoring invalid-workflow error for an unknown scripted step; simple message passthrough (preserve the exact text), mirroring `WorkflowNotFoundError`.\n2. `src/rebar/_errors.py`: add `WorkflowUnknownStepError` to the `invalid_input` group in `_workflow_caller_code` (extends the existing isinstance tuple — no new branch, no complexity increase). Update the docstring/comment.\n3. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py`: raise `WorkflowUnknownStepError(...)` instead of the bare base, preserving the message; import it.\n4. Held-out regression test (new): assert the executor unknown-step classifies as `invalid_input` through `error_code_for` AND `_structured_llm_failure` (and `!= llm_unavailable`), and that the bare `WorkflowError` execute base + genuine outages STILL map to `llm_unavailable` (AC3 unchanged).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AC1: An unknown scripted `uses:` step (executor.py:541) classifies as `invalid_input`, not `llm_unavailable`, via `error_code_for` and the `_structured_llm_failure` LLM-tier surface.\n- [ ] AC2: The bare `WorkflowError` execute base and genuine LLM outages (`LLMUnavailableError`, `LLMError`) still classify as `llm_unavailable` (dbca AC3 preserved).\n- [ ] AC3: The emitted code is a member of `rebar.KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`; no new vocabulary added.\n- [ ] AC4: Held-out RED→GREEN regression test asserts on the error CODE (not message text) and had teeth (mutation returns it to RED).\n\n## Split-out siblings (escalated design decisions — NOT in this ticket)\n- **551b-1a30-ac2b-4127** (sanidine-cilium-eland): editor.py:475 missing-bundle `WorkflowError`. CLI-only (not MCP-exposed; the CLI prints the raw message and never classifies), so not observably misclassified; correct code needs a NEW-vocabulary design decision the operator directed to escalate.\n- **73d8-4871-1b49-4047** (brainy-convulsant-unicorn): `ExpressionError` (execute-time workflow wiring) also classifies as `llm_unavailable`; whether to reclassify an execute-time expression fault is a design decision.\n\nOrigin: caused_by 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239 (blanket LLMError→llm_unavailable), class plan_defect — same as dbca.","title":"Bare WorkflowError at executor unknown-step misclassifies as llm_unavailable (should be invalid_input)"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788045381624991241,"uuid":"144af905-ac8d-4632-8a25-a19ee95f056f"}